  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/assets/a0674c068305434109322c2ade681279f11b78944356d7663198f9bfbf9cf962.png)\n\nLet $U={10,20,30,40,50}$ be the universal set and let $Q={10,30,40}.$ What is $\\overset{\u2015}{Q}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $Q,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{Q},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $Q.$ To represent $\\overset{\u2015}{Q},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $Q,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/assets/a29068d63563404b495e603e473a990186fed086439318d9ac26685b9474f331.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $20$ and $50.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $Q.$ Therefore, the complement of $Q$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{Q}={20,50}.\n$$",
